Barracuda entered service in 1943 as a replacement Fairey Albacore biplane, and after the retirement of the Blackburn Skua, it was the only British naval aircraft fit for dive bombing, even though it was primarily designed for torpedo bombing. Later models such as the Mk II and Mk III were radar-equipped and mostly used in anti-submarine operations. The Barracuda was used in numerous operations during the war, most famously in the attack on Tirpitz in Operation Tungsten, and was deployed in the Atlantic Ocean, Mediterranean Sea and the Pacific Ocean. A total of 2,602 aircraft were built from 1941-1945, including variants.","LocalizedString":"The Fairey Barracuda was a British carrier-borne torpedo and dive bomber that was used by the Royal Navy Fleet Air Arm (FAA) during WWII. The Barracuda entered service in 1943 as a replacement Fairey Albacore biplane, and after the retirement of the Blackburn Skua, it was the only British naval aircraft fit for dive bombing, even though it was primarily designed for torpedo bombing. Later models such as the Mk II and Mk III were radar-equipped and mostly used in anti-submarine operations. The Barracuda was used in numerous operations during the war, most famously in the attack on Tirpitz in Operation Tungsten, and was deployed in the Atlantic Ocean, Mediterranean Sea and the Pacific Ocean. A total of 2,602 aircraft were built from 1941-1945, including variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment","EHelpBubbleTypes::Pin"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'au_aircraft_large'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/au_aircraft_large.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Invasion/t_barracuda_unit.t_barracuda_unit","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::BotMid","artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPh